                <pb facs="0331" n="323" sameAs="frus:frus1938v01/pg323"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.2221/1185a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Bullitt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-09-28T17:00:00-05:00">September 28, 1938—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>714. Friends of the Abraham Lincoln Brigade inform us that French refuse to
                    permit entry into France of members of the International Brigade now being
                    discharged in conformity with Negrín’s announcement to the League and that
                    Amariglio will communicate with the Embassy in this regard.</p>
                <p>Please report by telegraph regarding this situation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
